Report the reason when readlink -v -f fails.
Only the failure to read a link was reported with -v. When -f could not
canonicalize the path, readlink exited with status 1 without a message,
even with -v. Print the error, as GNU readlink does. Without -v it is
still suppressed.

---
 coreutils/readlink.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/coreutils/readlink.c
+++ b/coreutils/readlink.c
@@ -81,6 +81,8 @@
 	/* NOFORK: only one alloc is allowed; must free */
 	if (opt & 2) { /* -f */
 		buf = xmalloc_realpath_coreutils(argv[optind]);
+		if (!buf)
+			bb_simple_perror_msg(argv[optind]);
 	} else {
 		buf = xmalloc_readlink_or_warn(argv[optind]);
 	}
